# What this package tracks is the instrument, not the runs.
#
# A clean clone plus `npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm test` must be enough to use the
# workflow. Everything needed for that is tracked: runtime/, scripts/, schemas/,
# tests/ (including the positive and negative control fixtures), vendor/, the
# normative documents, and the lockfile.
#
# Run outputs are not tracked. `README.md` already lists both directories below under
# "Not required (artifacts and temporary files)", and `npm run intake:batch` scaffolds
# `batches/<batch-id>/evaluation-config.mjs` itself with correct paths and hashes, so a
# cloner does not need a committed example of one.
#
# That includes `records/`. It holds the per-round work no script regenerates — the
# annotation-only copy, the adapter, the private policy, the frozen plan and its result —
# curated out of `generated/` by `npm run retain:round -- archive <game-id> <eval-id>`, so
# that `retain:round -- prune` can drop the bulk private evidence without losing it. That
# separation is what the tree is for; it is still a run output, not the instrument, so it
# is not tracked either. Back it up outside git if a working copy must survive.

node_modules/
tmp/

# Per-run evaluation workspace: frozen source pairs, adapters, private policies, frozen
# plans, artifacts, and results, one tree per game per evaluation id. 253 MB for one
# game across seven rounds.
generated/

# Per-run evaluation configs and ranking outputs. These import from generated/, so they
# are only meaningful alongside the workspace that intake created.
batches/

# Curated per-round agent work, see above.
records/
